{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Delete}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Delete}
\pard \fs36 Delete
\par \fs24 This function deletes the selected image file.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Filename filter}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} OHXACJ}
\pard \fs36 Filename filter
\par \fs24 
\par The files displayed in the gallery are subjected to a filename filter, default *.TIF
\par 
\par You may modify this using the Menu function \b File - Filter\plain\fs24 , which displays the filter dialog.
\par 
\par Use the wildcards * and ? to define the required filter.
\par e.g. File??? or File*
\par 
\par Note: The extension  \b .TIF\plain\fs24 . is always added to the filter you supply.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Gallery File}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Gallery_File}
\pard \fs36 Gallery File
\par \fs24 A Gallery file is a cache of \ul thumbnail images\plain\fs24 {\v 18H9TRS}.
\par When the Gallery is opened the program attempts to open a gallery file \b Gallery.Gal\plain\fs24  in the image directory.
\par The Gallery file may not be present for two reasons:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 1. This is the first time the Image Gallery has been used. A Gallery file will be created when the Gallery is closed.
\par 2. The Image Directory may be \b read only\plain\fs24  (e.g. it may be on a CD-ROM). If this is the case a Gallery file may have been created in the User Directory.
\par 
\par If images have been created/Deleted since the Gallery was opened \ul refresh\plain\fs24 {\v Refresh} the display.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Load Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Load_Image}
\pard \fs36 Gallery Load Image
\par \fs24 
\par An Image may be loaded from the Gallery by double clicking on it.
\par Alternatively Load may be selected from the \uldb popup menu\plain\fs24 {\v Pop_up_menu} or \uldb Drag and drop\plain\fs24 {\v Drag_and_Drop} may be used
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Multiple selection}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Multiple_selection}
\pard \fs36 Multiple selection
\par \fs24 Multiple images may be selected by holding down the Ctrl key while selecting the image.
\par 
\par Up to 6 images may be selected in this manner.
\par 
\par Multiple images may be \ul printed\plain\fs24 {\v Printing_multiple_images}.
\par 
\par See also \uldb Drag and drop\plain\fs24 {\v Drag_and_Drop}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Overview}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1375BLH}
\pard \fs36 Image Gallery Overview
\par \fs24 
\par The Image Gallery presents the user with a display of \ul thumbnail representations\plain\fs24 {\v 18H9TRS} of the images in the current image directory.
\par 
\par A \ul Gallery File\plain\fs24 {\v Gallery_File} is used to speed up display of thumbnail images.
\par 
\par True colour images are excluded from the Gallery.
\par 
\par The files displayed may be subjected to a \ul filename filter\plain\fs24 {\v OHXACJ}.
\par 
\par An Image may be \ul selected\plain\fs24 {\v Select_File} and it's properties displayed.
\par 
\par Double click on an image for Image import load
\par \pard 
\par \ul Multiple\plain\fs24 {\v Multiple_selection} images may be selected for \ul printing\plain\fs24 {\v Printing_multiple_images} on a single sheet
\par 
\par Right Mouse click on a thumbnail for \ul pop up menu\plain\fs24 {\v Pop_up_menu}
\par 
\par Files may be \uldb dragged\plain\fs24 {\v Drag_and_Drop} to other windows
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Pop up menu}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Pop_up_menu}
\pard \fs36 Gallery pop up menu
\par \fs24 Right mouse button click displays the menu \{bmc bm0.bmp\} and selects the thumbnail
\par 
\par \ul Property\plain\fs24 {\v CX.Z7}
\par \b Print \plain\fs24 will print the image on the Default Windows Printer
\par \b Load\plain\fs24  will load the selected image
\par \b Delete\plain\fs24  will delete the selected file
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Printing multiple images}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Printing_multiple_images}
\pard \fs36 Printing multiple images
\par \fs24 The menu function \b File - Print\plain\fs24  will print the currently selected images (from 1 to 6 images) to the default printer.
\par 
\par All the images are printed on the same page.
\par 
\par The size and layout of the images depends on the number of images selected. All images are normalised to the same size such that they fit a single page in Landscape/Portrait.
\par 
\par Note that each image printed is a spatially reduced version of the TIFF file, there are no changes to magnification values to reflect the actual printed image size.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Properties}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} CX.Z7}
\pard \fs36 Properties
\par \fs24 The properties of the \ul selected\plain\fs24 {\v Select_File} file may be displayed using the menu function \b File - Properties\plain\fs24 . 
\par The properties displayed are 
\par \pard\tx355 \tab Height
\par \tab Width
\par \tab Date/Time
\par \tab Filesize
\par \tab User text
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Refresh}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Refresh}
\pard\tx355 \fs36 Refresh
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 This menu function (\b File - Refresh\plain\fs24 ) of the Image gallery refreshes the \ul Gallery file\plain\fs24 {\v Gallery_File} by comparing it's contents with the image directory.
\par \pard\tx355 Any files which have been deleted are removed and any files which have changed are replaced with new \ul thumbnails\plain\fs24 {\v 18H9TRS}.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Select File}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Select_File}
\pard \fs36 Select File
\par \fs24 To select a file position the cursor over the \ul thumbnail\plain\fs24 {\v 18H9TRS} required and click the left mouse button. 
\par A Border is drawn around the selected image.
\par 
\par The \ul properties\plain\fs24 {\v CX.Z7} of the selected file may be displayed.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Thumbnail}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 18H9TRS}
\pard \fs36 Thumbnail 
\par \fs24 A Thumbnail representation of an image is the image file spatially reduced to fit within a 128 * 96 pixel area for display in the Gallery.
\par The file name is displayed below the thumbnail.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Drag and Drop}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Drag_and_Drop}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Delete;Drag and Drop;Filename filter;Gallery File;Load Image;Multiple selection}
\fs36 Drag and Drop
\par \fs24 Files in the Image Gallery may be dragged and dropped onto other Windows, including those of other applications. See \uldb \b Drag and Drop\plain\b\fs24 {\v Drag_and_Drop@sem.hlp}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par To drag an image select the Thumbnail required by holding the left mouse button down on it and drag it to its destination (e.g. The SEM Image Window)  then release the mouse button. The image will be loaded to the image store.
\par 
\par Other Drop targets are the \uldb \b Second Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v 4AHWGBN@tabmgr.hlp}, \plain\fs24 Microsoft Word document windows\b  \plain\fs24 and Windows Explorer (Directory).
\par \pard 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Note:\plain\fs24  if dropping into the Explorer the files will be\b  Moved\plain\fs24 , unless the \b <Ctrl>\plain\fs24  Key is held down before the drop.
\par \b Note:\plain\fs24  If Multiple files are to be dragged then drag the \b last\plain\fs24  selected thumbnail. 
\par \page
